<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Habr Yunis</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Habr Yunis are a major clan of the Isaaq clan family of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> people, living mainly in the Togdheer and Sahil regions of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a> and in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somali-region">Somali Region</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ethiopia">Ethiopia</a>. Around 1787 they formed their own sultanate, breaking away from the Isaaq Sultanate, and in the 1880s they signed protection treaties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. Their sultans were based near Toon and later around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burao">Burao</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/habr-yunis.jpg" alt="Habr Yunis" width="320" height="176" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Pitt · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Chieftains_of_the_Isaaq_clan_cropped.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
